Provide local stubs for ICU NumberFormatterSettings and
NumberRangeFormatterSettings ctor/dtor under clang/mingw.

ICU's <unicode/numberformatter.h> declares (extern template class
U_I18N_API NumberFormatterSettings<...>) and the same for
NumberRangeFormatterSettings, decorating the template members with
__declspec(dllimport) when using shared system ICU. Clang strictly
honours that: it emits __imp_*C2Ev / __imp_*D2Ev references for the
empty-bodied ctor/dtor of the affected template instantiations.

ICU itself never ships those particular symbols -- they are empty
= default and the optimizer drops them before the DLL export table --
so the link of mksnapshot.exe fails with five undefined references:

  __imp__ZN6icu_78number23NumberFormatterSettings
        INS0_26UnlocalizedNumberFormatterEEC2Ev  (and the D2Ev twin)
  __imp__ZN6icu_78number28NumberRangeFormatterSettings
        INS0_31UnlocalizedNumberRangeFormatterEEC2Ev  (and D2Ev twin)
  __imp__ZN6icu_78number28NumberRangeFormatterSettings
        INS0_29LocalizedNumberRangeFormatterEEC2Ev   (ctor only;
        the matching D2Ev is exported by libicuin.dll.a)

GCC instantiates these locally despite the dllimport tag and so never
asks for them.

Two halves are needed for the mingw fix:

  1. A real function with the Itanium-mangled name. This is what the
     indirect import-table call ultimately jumps to.
  2. A const data symbol __imp_<mangled> holding the address of the
     stub. The call site loads from __imp_<mangled> -- GNU ld does NOT
     synthesize this slot from a local function definition (auto-import
     covers DLL DATA imports only). v8 TUs (JSDurationFormat,
     JSPluralRules, JSNumberFormat::GetRangeFormatter) all go through
     the indirect __imp_* call, so the data slot must be explicit.

Both halves live in js-number-format.cc (already linked into every v8
build that touches Intl) under an __clang__ && __MINGW32__ guard so
the GCC build is untouched. The mangled name is version-locked to
icu_78 -- a future MSYS2 ICU bump will require updating the namespace
token in each line.

--- a/src/3rdparty/chromium/v8/src/objects/js-number-format.cc
+++ b/src/3rdparty/chromium/v8/src/objects/js-number-format.cc
@@ -2203,3 +2203,27 @@ const std::set<std::string>& JSNumberFormat::GetAvailableLocales() {

 }  // namespace internal
 }  // namespace v8
+
+#if defined(__clang__) && defined(__MINGW32__)
+// Resolve clang's __imp_* references to ICU template ctor/dtor that
+// libicuin.dll does not export. Each stub pairs a no-op function with
+// a const data symbol __imp_<mangled> pointing at it, since GNU ld
+// does not synthesize the import-table slot from a local function
+// definition (auto-import covers DLL DATA imports only).
+//
+// Namespace token icu_78 is encoded in the mangled name -- update on
+// MSYS2 ICU version bumps.
+#define V8_ICU_DLLIMPORT_STUB(mangled)                               \
+  extern "C" void mangled() {}                                       \
+  extern "C" void (*const __imp_##mangled)() = &mangled
+// NumberFormatterSettings<UnlocalizedNumberFormatter> ctor/dtor
+V8_ICU_DLLIMPORT_STUB(_ZN6icu_786number23NumberFormatterSettingsINS0_26UnlocalizedNumberFormatterEEC2Ev);
+V8_ICU_DLLIMPORT_STUB(_ZN6icu_786number23NumberFormatterSettingsINS0_26UnlocalizedNumberFormatterEED2Ev);
+// NumberRangeFormatterSettings<UnlocalizedNumberRangeFormatter> ctor/dtor
+V8_ICU_DLLIMPORT_STUB(_ZN6icu_786number28NumberRangeFormatterSettingsINS0_31UnlocalizedNumberRangeFormatterEEC2Ev);
+V8_ICU_DLLIMPORT_STUB(_ZN6icu_786number28NumberRangeFormatterSettingsINS0_31UnlocalizedNumberRangeFormatterEED2Ev);
+// NumberRangeFormatterSettings<LocalizedNumberRangeFormatter> ctor only
+// (the matching D2Ev is already exported by libicuin.dll.a).
+V8_ICU_DLLIMPORT_STUB(_ZN6icu_786number28NumberRangeFormatterSettingsINS0_29LocalizedNumberRangeFormatterEEC2Ev);
+#undef V8_ICU_DLLIMPORT_STUB
+#endif
